Revision history for RPi-DAC-MCP4922

3.1802 UNREL
    - Fixed inverted SHDN bit polarity in the SHUTDOWN BITS POD table (bit 12:
      1 = Active, 0 = Shutdown, matching DS22250A Reg 5-1 and the XS)
    - Added t/register.t: the dist's first functional tests - HW-free coverage
      of the pure XS word-builders (_reg_init BUF/GAIN/SHDN bits; __set_dac
      DAC-select bit 15 set/clear/preserve), the model->bits->lsb chain, the
      accessor/constructor validation croaks, and the register() accessor
    - Added ON THE WIRE and DATASHEET sections to TECHNICAL INFORMATION: the
      16-bit write frame diagrammed byte-by-byte with worked set() and
      disable_sw() examples, and a link to DS22250A
    - Fixed SHUTDOWN BITS POD prose: the register bit shuts down only the DAC
      selected by bit 15 (DS22250A Register 5-1), not both DACs; the hardware
      SHDN pin is what affects both
    - Bundled datasheet reference now points at docs/datasheet/mcp49xx.pdf
      (already shipped) instead of the web URL in the DATASHEET POD
    - Removed the unused docs/datasheet/mcp48xx.pdf (DS22244B, the MCP48xx
      internal-Vref family this module doesn't drive) and its MANIFEST entry
    - Added t/register.t to MANIFEST (was on disk but unlisted)
    - Fixed _set()'s clear-mask (XS): it cleared 0xFFF >> lsb (the low bits)
      rather than the full 12-bit data field, so stale bits in the top of the
      field could survive on the 8/10-bit models; it now clears bits 11-0
    - Dropped the dead "my $buf =" capture of the void _set() in set()
    - Reworded register()'s POD: it returns the cached construction-time
      register (BUF/GAIN/SHDN), not a live view of set() writes
    - Split the register-word assembly out of _set() (XS) into a pure
      __build_word() helper, and covered it in t/register.t across the
      8/10/12-bit lsb values (incl. stale-cache cases) so the clear-mask fix
      is verified without an 8/10-bit MCP4902/4912 part

3.1801    2026-06-12
        - Migrated constants from removed RPi::WiringPi::Constant to
          RPi::Const (incl. Makefile.PL prereq)
        - Bump prereq of WiringPi::API to 3.1801
        - Bump prereq of RPi::Const to 1.05

2.3605 2017-06-28
        - bump prereq ver of WiringPi::API to 2.3612
        - bump prereq ver of RPi::WiringPi::Constant to 1.00

2.3604  2017-03-13
        - changed versioning scheme from 2.36.x to 2.360x in module and prereqs

2.36.3  2017-02-22
        - WiringPi::API prereq now v2.36.6, as that distribution was updated to
          correct a few build/installation issues

2.36.2  2017-02-21
        - renamed one of the datasheets (mcp48**.pdf to mcp48xx.pdf) due to
          the package not being able to be unpackaged on Win32 platforms
          (reported by Alexandr Ciornii) (closes #1)
        - brought version up to par with the rest of the RPi modules that
          require wiringPi C libs
        - forgot to modify changes for the proper version (d'oh!)

0.01    2017-02-01
        First version, released on an unsuspecting world.

